All seven technical gates are now complete. The proof is fresh, result-constraining, non-vacuous, and pinned to the actual translated body; nevertheless, it proves the wrong behavior on an unrestricted source-domain input because the generated semantics replaces Python’s Unicode-aware `str.lower()` with ASCII-only lowering. I’m consolidating the exact rule inventory, trust ledger, and verdict rationale in `REVIEW.md`.
